utes car and pi when we return we  simply return  this dot state dot car and this dot  state  dot by now this is how you would create  stateful components and access the state  properties within the view how do you  update the state of a component  by using the built-in set state method  you can go ahead and update the state  of the component so here we have a  simple render function that returns  the state itself state dot message and  on the on click connects to a button  press  function the moment you click on the  button the button press function  sets the state to another message so the  initial message in the constructor is  welcome to simply learn  the moment you click on the button the  set state triggers and changes it  to best place to learn so the data on  the view would be  updated what are props in react well  props is just a short  form for properties and that is what  allows us to pass arguments or  data to a component props are passed to  components  in the way similar to that of attributes  that are passed to an html element  so how do you pass props between two  components so let's say we have an  app.js component on the top and a  main.js component  at the bottom at the top we are trying  to return this dot props dot  car and the pike so two car and bike  attributes  associated with this props of the app  component in the main component when you  look at the render function  we are associating car prop equal to a  value of 1 600 cc and bike prop  equal to value of 150cc  and to access it if you look at the  import statement we are importing app  from app.jsx and this is how you can  cross-access  properties from one component within the  other so what are the difference between  state and props  well state holds information about the  components they are mutable they can be  changed  they cannot be accessed by child  components and they cannot  have state props allow to pass data from  one component to the other  as an argument they are immutable they  are read only and props can be accessed  by the child component and they can  have props as well what is a higher  order component in react so these act as  a container  for other components which helps in  keeping components simple  and induces the reusability factor  they are generally used when a common  logic has to be used by multiple  components that's when you group  together a set of components within a  higher order  component in react how can you embed two  or more components  into one this code snippet demonstrates  the app component which returns  a hello text and it has a custom tag  called simple  the simple tag is defined in the  component below and it returns  text called simply learn and in the  render of the react dom  we simply go and render the app  component so hello  simply learn would be the final output  and that's how you can embed  one component into the other using this  methodology what are the differences  between class and functional components  so stateful components would extend  react component in this case  and if you could look at the render it  simply renders this.props.title  the constant stateless component would  be equal to props  the div tag returns this dot props dot  title so you can look at the style  very different in terms of class and  functional components  one using the arrow operator one using  the traditional class and render method  so the class component can hold or  manage state  complex as compared to stateless  components can work  all of the life cycle methods of the  component and it can be reused  the functional component cannot hold a  managed state they are simple and easy  to understand it does not work with any  life cycle method and it cannot be  reused  let's explain the lifecycle methods of  components we've got kennish initial  state  which is executed before the creation of  the component  component did mount which is executed  when the component gets rendered and  placed on the dom  should component update which is invoked  when a component decides  any changes to the dom and returns true  or false  value based on certain conditions  component did update  it is invoked immediately after the  rendering takes place  component will unmount which is invoked  immediately before a component is  destroyed and unmounted  permanently let's move to the react  redux set of questions  so what is redux it's an open source  javascript library used to manage  application state and react uses redux  for building the user  interface what are components of redux  the first  is the store which holds the state of  the application store contains state  which defines the user interface which  triggers a set of actions which are then  sent  to the reducer so store holds the state  action is the source information for the  store and reducer specifies how the  application state changes  in response to actions sent to the store  what is flux  well flux is the application  architecture that facebook uses for  building  web applications and it works in this  way the action is triggered which is  sent to the dispatcher the dispatcher  sends it to the store  the store sends it to the view and the  view  sends it back to the action and that's  exactly how the steps would continue in  sequence  so when we trigger an action the  dispatcher will get notified once the  dispatcher has dealt with an action the  stores  listening to it will get triggered the  view gets updated when the state  of the store changes user action at the  view  is sent to the dispatcher to then be  processed how is redux different  from flux redux is an open source  javascript library used to manage  application state  the store state is immutable it can only  have a single store  and it uses the concept of reducer flux  on the other hand is an architecture and  not a framework or library  the store state is mutable it can have  multiple stores  and it uses the concept of dispatcher  let's look at some react  router questions what is a react router  a react router is a package which is  used to create routing in a react  application  react router is used for developing  single page web applications it allows  multiple views  in a single application by defining  multiple routes  in that react application how is react  routing different from conventional  routing  react routing has a single html page it  uses  or the end user rather would navigate  multiple views  within the same file called a single  page app the page does not refresh since  it's a single page file  and there is improved performance since  you are not navigating across multiple  pages  conventional routing each view is a  separate html file the user would  navigate  multiple files for each view the page  would refresh  every time the user navigates which  would hence result in slower performance  how do you implement react routing you  can implement react routing  using a very simple method considering  the above components  let's say you've got a component called  app about and contact  so here you can specify the route path  if the route part  is just slash the route defaults out it  takes you to the app component  if the route is slash about in the url  given by the end user you automatically  navigate and activate and load  the about component and if the url is  slash contact it would take you to the  contact component  let's talk about react styling questions  how do you style react components  either you use inline styling by using  simple css  by simply saying color blue and that's  going to be the output of the h1  element or i could use a javascript  object by  specifying a constant simple style  object and specifying a keypair value of  color  background color margin font family and  apply that object  as the style parameter which would  result in this  styled output how do you style react  components using a css style sheet so  here's an external style sheet so we've  written all the styling rules in a  separate css  file app.css we've imported that at the  top of the  app.js react class and lo and behold you  have the output  simplified as generated on your page  let's explain the use  of css modules in react so a css module  file  is created.module.css is the  extension the css inside a module file  is available only for the component that  is  importing it so there are no naming  conflicts so dot button  is the css styling inside  button.module.css  and that is what we've imported from in  the app.js file so when you view the  button  style start button is the styling picked  up from the button.module.css  file file alright so that is it for this  complete react crash course  if you liked the video give it a thumbs  up and hit the subscribe button and the  bell icons  to never miss an update thank you for  being here keep learning and stay tuned  to simply learn  [Music]  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel  and click here to watch similar videos  turn it up and get certified  click here  you
 

